      "id": "ec9dcda5-10e1-45e2-a9f9-643400bf6f05",
      "name": "CV Readable?"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=CANDIDATE CV:\n\n{{ $json.cv_text }}\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION:\n\n{{ $('Prepare Application Data').item.json.job_description }}\n\nCandidate: {{ $('Prepare Application Data').item.json.candidate_name }}\nCompany: {{ $('Prepare Application Data').item.json.company }}\nPosition: {{ $('Prepare Application Data').item.json.job_title }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=You are an expert technical recruiter and evidence-based CV evaluation system.\n\nYour task is to evaluate the candidate CV against the provided Job Description.\n\nIMPORTANT RULES:\n\n1. Use ONLY information explicitly present in the CV and Job Description.\n2. NEVER invent skills, experience, projects, certifications, education, achievements, tools, or responsibilities.\n3. Every score MUST be supported by evidence from the CV.\n4. If something is not found in the CV, mark it as \"Not Found\".\n5. Do not assume that a candidate knows a technology just because they know a related technology.\n6. Do not give points for unsupported claims.\n7. Separate \"Matched\", \"Partial Match\", and \"Not Found\".\n8. Calculate the final score from the weighted criteria below.\n9. The final score MUST equal the sum of all criterion scores.\n10. Maximum total score is exactly 100.\n\nSCORING RUBRIC:\n\n1. Core / Required Skills = 30 points\n2. Relevant Experience = 20 points\n3. Projects / Practical Work = 15 points\n4. Education / Degree = 10 points\n5. Job Responsibilities Match = 10 points\n6. Certifications = 5 points\n7. Tools / Technologies = 5 points\n8. ATS / Important JD Terminology = 5 points\n\nTOTAL = 100 POINTS\n\nSCORING RULES:\n\nCORE SKILLS — 30 POINTS\n- Identify the important required skills from the Job Description.\n- Compare each requirement against the CV.\n- Give points only when the CV provides evidence.\n- Distinguish exact matches from partial matches.\n- Record proof for every important skill.\n\nRELEVANT EXPERIENCE — 20 POINTS\n- Evaluate internships, employment, training, or other explicitly stated professional experience.\n- Consider relevance to the target position.\n- Do not treat academic knowledge as professional experience.\n\nPROJECTS / PRACTICAL WORK — 15 POINTS\n- Evaluate projects explicitly mentioned in the CV.\n- Consider relevance, technical complexity, and technologies used.\n- Projects can provide evidence of practical ability but must not be treated as employment experience.\n\nEDUCATION — 10 POINTS\n- Compare the candidate's degree, field, and education against the Job Description.\n- Give points based only on explicit CV information.\n\nJOB RESPONSIBILITIES — 10 POINTS\n- Compare responsibilities in the Job Description with activities explicitly demonstrated in the CV.\n- Give higher scores when the CV provides direct evidence.\n\nCERTIFICATIONS — 5 POINTS\n- Only count certifications explicitly listed in the CV.\n- Do not assume certification from experience with a technology.\n\nTOOLS / TECHNOLOGIES — 5 POINTS\n- Compare tools and technologies required by the Job Description with those explicitly present in the CV.\n\nATS / JD TERMINOLOGY — 5 POINTS\n- Evaluate important terminology and keywords from the Job Description that are genuinely supported by the CV.\n- Do not reward keyword stuffing without evidence.\n\nEVIDENCE REQUIREMENT:\n\nFor every scoring criterion provide:\n- score\n- maximum score\n- reason\n- matched items\n- partial matches\n- missing items\n- proof\n\nProof must quote or closely identify the relevant information from the CV.\n\nFor missing information use:\n\"Not found in the provided CV.\"\n\nFINAL SCORE:\n\nCalculate:\n\ncore_skills_score\n+ experience_score\n+ projects_score\n+ education_score\n+ responsibilities_score\n+ certifications_score\n+ tools_score\n+ ats_score\n\nThe result must be exactly between 0 and 100.\n\nAlso calculate a confidence score from 0 to 100 representing how strongly the final evaluation is supported by explicit CV evidence.\n\nDo not confuse confidence with fit score.\n\nFinally:\n- provide matching skills\n- provide missing skills\n- provide detailed reasoning\n- generate a personalized cover letter\n- never invent information.\n\nCOVER LETTER REQUIREMENTS:\n\n- Address the letter to the hiring team at the named company.\n- Reference the exact job title.\n- Use only achievements, skills, projects and experience that appear in the CV.\n- Explicitly connect two or three CV items to specific requirements in the Job Description.\n- Length: 250 to 350 words.\n- Professional tone, no placeholder text such as [Your Name] or [Company].\n- Do not mention the fit score, the rubric, or that the letter was AI generated.\n- Return plain text with paragraph breaks, no markdown formatting.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT:\n\nReturn a single valid JSON object matching the required schema. Return nothing else.\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        1360,
        256
      ],
      "id": "7f8f5674-b4d2-4504-99c5-220d5426950d",
      "name": "AI - Score Fit & Write Cover Letter",
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 3000,
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsonSchemaExample": "{\n  \"fit_score\": 85,\n  \"confidence\": 92,\n\n  \"fit_summary\": \"Short explanation of the candidate's overall suitability.\",\n\n  \"score_breakdown\": {\n    \"core_skills\": {\n      \"score\": 27,\n      \"max_score\": 30,\n      \"reason\": \"Strong match with most required skills.\",\n      \"matched\": [\n        {\n          \"requirement\": \"Python\",\n          \"status\": \"Matched\",\n          \"proof\": \"Python listed under Technical Skills.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"partial_matches\": [],\n      \"missing\": [\n        {\n          \"requirement\": \"Kubernetes\",\n          \"status\": \"Not Found\",\n          \"proof\": \"Not found in the provided CV.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n\n    \"experience\": {\n      \"score\": 16,\n      \"max_score\": 20,\n      \"reason\": \"Relevant internship experience is present.\",\n      \"proof\": [\n        \"Machine Learning internship experience is explicitly listed in the CV.\"\n      ]\n    },\n\n    \"projects\": {\n      \"score\": 14,\n      \"max_score\": 15,\n      \"reason\": \"Projects demonstrate relevant practical skills.\",\n      \"proof\": [\n        \"Relevant technical projects are explicitly listed in the CV.\"\n      ]\n    },\n\n    \"education\": {\n      \"score\": 10,\n      \"max_score\": 10,\n      \"reason\": \"Education matches the job requirement.\",\n      \"proof\": [\n        \"Candidate degree is explicitly listed in the CV.\"\n      ]\n    },\n\n    \"responsibilities\": {\n      \"score\": 8,\n      \"max_score\": 10,\n      \"reason\": \"Most responsibilities are supported by CV evidence.\",\n      \"proof\": []\n    },\n\n    \"certifications\": {\n      \"score\": 2,\n      \"max_score\": 5,\n      \"reason\": \"Some relevant certification evidence is present.\",\n      \"proof\": []\n    },\n\n    \"tools\": {\n      \"score\": 4,\n      \"max_score\": 5,\n      \"reason\": \"Most required tools are present.\",\n      \"proof\": []\n    },\n\n    \"ats_keywords\": {\n      \"score\": 4,\n      \"max_score\": 5,\n      \"reason\": \"Most important terminology is supported by the CV.\",\n      \"proof\": []\n    }\n  },\n\n  \"matching_skills\": [\n    \"Python\",\n    \"FastAPI\"\n  ],\n\n  \"missing_skills\": [\n    \"Kubernetes\"\n  ],\n\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"Python\",\n      \"status\": \"Matched\",\n      \"proof\": \"Python is explicitly listed in the candidate's technical skills.\"\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"reasoning\": \"Detailed explanation of how the final score was calculated using only CV evidence.\",\n\n  \"cover_letter\": \"Personalized professional cover letter.\"\n}"
      },
